From 1e339d9ec3ec2d669a14d41c430aeaa1b8d443ac Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: daveey <daveey@users.noreply.github.com>
Date: Wed, 28 Oct 2026 14:15:11 +0000
Subject: [PATCH] fix(tui): a chat held by another backend gets one refusal
 notice, not a retry loop [daveey]

A synthesized turn (process completion, subagent result, /loop tick, kanban notice) refused SESSION_NOT_OWNED
because another backend holds the chat's durable turn lease went straight back on the queue, and the
notification poller re-ran it on its next pass. Each refused attempt painted "Hermes hit an internal error
... Your message was not answered" (139 cards in 110 s, David-MBP 2026-10-28, chat 20261023_204423_b85a94,
until hermes-sync's drain closed admission).

- _admit_prompt_turn records the refusal code on the session; _notif_run_submit reads it and starts a
  doubling backoff (30 s up to 300 s). _notif_claim_turn claims nothing while it holds.
- Inside a refusal streak, a retry probes ownership first and stays silent while the chat is still held,
  so the user sees exactly one notice per streak. A successful admission clears the streak.
- A refused completion event is released and held for this chat instead of being marked delivered with no
  turn run; it is delivered once the other backend lets go.
- SESSION_NOT_OWNED / SESSION_COORDINATION_UNAVAILABLE get their own turn-error copy ("This chat is open in
  another Hermes window or device") instead of the gateway layer's "internal error".

Tests: tests/tui_gateway/test_notification_owner_refusal_backoff.py (real poller thread + admission against a
foreign lease: bounded attempts and one notice; delivered after release; user prompts still refuse every
time) and tests/e2e/core/terminal/test_held_session_notification_refusal.py (real `hermes serve`, background
job completing while a second process holds the durable turn lease: 111 attempts/111 cards in 40 s before,
1/1 after).
